{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/testing/architecture/http-endpoint-ownership","title":"Unique HTTP endpoint ownership","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"unique-http-endpoint-ownership","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Unique HTTP endpoint ownership"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"assertHttpEndpointUnique"},{"t":"text","text":" treats an HTTP endpoint as the pair of its method and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"URL. It fails when two graph sites call the same pair:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"function","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"keepEndpointOwnershipUnique","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"graph"},{"text":":","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"ArchitectureGraph","kind":"type"},{"text":") {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"assertHttpEndpointUnique","kind":"function"},{"text":"(graph.graph);","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"}","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-it-prevents","children":[{"t":"text","text":"What it prevents"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Two services can independently implement this:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"CraftHttpClient.","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"get","kind":"function"},{"text":"(({ ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"response"},{"text":" }) ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"=>","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ({","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  url: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'users'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":",","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  success: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"response","kind":"function"},{"text":"<","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"User","kind":"type"},{"text":"[]>(),","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"}));","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"typescript","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The application still compiles, but there are now two owners for "},{"t":"code","text":"GET users"},{"t":"text","text":"."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"One may add pagination, the other may keep an old response shape. A bug fix in"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"one call site does not reach the other."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The rule forces a single boundary service to own "},{"t":"code","text":"GET users"},{"t":"text","text":". Other services"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"depend on that service and can derive feature-specific views without creating a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"second transport contract."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-counts-as-distinct","children":[{"t":"text","text":"What counts as distinct"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"These are separate endpoints and are allowed:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"GET  users"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"POST users"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"GET  orders"}]}],"filename":"","language":"","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The rule is intentionally narrower than “one URL in the whole app”: a read and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"a write are different contracts."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"why-this-is-graph-wide","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Why this is graph-wide"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"ESLint can flag a local HTTP style mistake. It cannot see that a second feature"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"has claimed an endpoint already owned elsewhere. The graph can inspect every"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"call site in one assertion."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"see-also","children":[{"t":"text","text":"See also"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","chi